{
  "info": {
    "name": "authservice - Seed test accounts",
    "description": "Run this folder in the Collection Runner (or `postman collection run <file> -i \"Seed test accounts (one-click)\"`)\nto create and approve one account per role. Every account uses the password in `{{seedPassword}}`.\n\n| Role | Email | clientId |\n|---|---|---|\n| SUPER_ADMIN | superadmin@uyir.test | superadmin-portal |\n| ADMIN | admin@uyir.test | admin-portal |\n| PATIENT | patient@uyir.test | patient-app |\n| DOCTOR | doctor@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| HOSPITAL | hospital@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| LS | ls@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| AMBULANCE_DRIVER | ambulance-driver@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| PRO | pro@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| LSC | lsc@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| ECG | ecg@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| HP | hp@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| HBC | hbc@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| TCS | tcs@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n\nSafe to re-run: existing accounts return 409 (counted as OK) and only PENDING `@uyir.test` accounts get approved.\nApproving is done by the Super Admin, so nobody else's pending account is touched.\n\nThe run makes 14 calls to the auth rate limiter (13 registers + 1 login). The default limit is\n20 per 15 minutes per IP, so a second run straight after the first will get 429s - wait, or\nstart the server with a higher `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000"
    },
    {
      "key": "seedPassword",
      "value": "Uyir@12345"
    },
    {
      "key": "seedSuperAdminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "seedPendingIds",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "seedApproveId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "loginChallengeId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "loginOtp",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
